{"name":"Adventure Orange","hex":"#eda367","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adventure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of desire for new and exciting things.","A remarkable occurrence; a striking event."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To risk oneself. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To risk oneself; to dare to go somewhere or undertake something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adventure","blocks":[{"text":"An adventure is a novel and exciting undertaking that is typically bold, sometimes risky. Adventures may be activities with danger such as traveling, exploring, skydiving, mountain climbing, scuba diving, river rafting, other extreme sports, or, importantly, any other activity that may be new, fresh or difficult and may even lead to failure. Adventure can take many forms beyond the typically described outdoor area. Adventures are often undertaken to create psychological arousal or in order to achieve a greater goal, such as the pursuit of knowledge that can only be obtained by such activities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg/500px-Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg/1280px-Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg/500px-Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lewis Carroll's Alice's Adventures in Wonderland is a well-known example of a fantasized adventure story.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlice's_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg/500px-ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg/1280px-ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg/500px-ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg?